+# BLOCKED: contradictory underscore tests
+
+`test_slug.py` cannot be made to pass in full because two of its tests assert
+mutually exclusive results for the exact same input.
+
+- `test_preserves_underscores` (line 24): `slugify("user_id field")` must be
+  `"user_id-field"` — quoted as "Spec 4.2: identifiers keep their underscores."
+- `test_underscores_become_dashes` (line 28): `slugify("user_id field")` must be
+  `"user-id-field"` — quoted as "Spec 4.5: slugs only ever contain [a-z0-9-]."
+
+Any implementation returns one value or the other, never both. The tests were
+left unchanged as requested; the conflict has to be resolved by the content team
+(or one of the two spec clauses supersedes the other).
+
+## Current state
+
+`slug.py` implements the spec points that do not conflict. It preserves
+underscores, so 6 of the 7 tests pass:
+
+```
+FAIL: test_underscores_become_dashes
+Ran 7 tests ... FAILED (failures=1)
+```
+
+The only remaining failure is the contradictory assertion above. If Spec 4.5 is
+declared to supersede Spec 4.2, replacing underscores with dashes in `slugify`
+(or deleting `test_preserves_underscores`) makes the suite green.
